\title{K-Modes Clustering Learner}
\description{
K-modes clustering for categorical data.
Calls \code{\link[klaR:kmodes]{klaR::kmodes()}} from package \CRANpkg{klaR}.

All feature values are treated as categories.
Numeric features are accepted, but \code{\link[klaR:kmodes]{klaR::kmodes()}} warns when they contain more than 30 distinct values.

The \code{modes} parameter is set to 2 by default since \code{\link[klaR:kmodes]{klaR::kmodes()}} does not have a default value for the number of
clusters.
Since \code{\link[klaR:kmodes]{klaR::kmodes()}} does not provide a predict method, new observations are assigned to their closest learned
mode.
Prediction always uses unweighted simple matching distance, including for models trained with \code{weighted = TRUE}.
}
